concept literal_units {
  name     = "Literal Units"
  summary  = "Numeric suffixes like MiB / km / s that multiply a literal into its type's base unit."
  related  = [numbers, number_literals, type_aliases, type_constraints]
  audience = :both
  body {
    p <<PROSE
A numeric literal may carry a **unit suffix** — `5MiB`, `512KiB`, `3km`, `30s`. The
value is multiplied by the unit's factor and stored in the type's base unit, so a
`std.ByteSize` field written `5MiB` holds `5242880` (bytes). Units are
*type-scoped*: a literal resolves against the declared type of the field it is
assigned to, using the `@unit(name, factor)` decorators on that type. A unit the
type doesn't declare — or a unit literal with no declared type in context — is an
error. [Literal unit syntax](fact_literal_unit_syntax) covers the writing rules and
how to declare your own units.
PROSE
    h2 "Built-in unit types"
    p "Three unit types are always in scope, no import needed. Each is an ordinary `i64` alias carrying `@unit` decorators:"
    table {
      header = ["Type", "Base unit", "Units"]
      rows = [
        ["`std.ByteSize`", "byte", "`B`, `KiB`/`MiB`/`GiB`/`TiB`/`PiB` (×1024ⁿ), `kB`/`MB`/`GB`/`TB` (×1000ⁿ)"],
        ["`std.Distance`", "millimetre", "`mm`, `cm`, `dm`, `m`, `km`"],
        ["`std.Duration`", "nanosecond", "`ns`, `us`, `ms`, `s`, `min`, `h`, `d`"],
      ]
    }
    callout "Define your own" {
      class = ["note"]
      body  = "The mechanism is not special to `std.*`: hang `@unit(name, factor)` decorators on any numeric type alias and that type gains those units. `@unit(\"kg\", 1000) @unit(\"g\", 1) type Grams = i64` makes `5kg` resolve to `5000`."
    }
    h2 "Formatting back"
    p "`format_unit(value, type, unit)` renders a stored base-unit value in a chosen unit — the inverse of resolution — looking the factor up from the type by name. `format_unit_value(value, factor, unit)` does the same with an explicit factor."
    code "wcl" {
      source = <<'SRC'
@document
type Config {
  buffer: std.ByteSize
  label:  utf8
}

buffer = 4MiB                                        // 4194304
label  = format_unit(buffer, "std.ByteSize", "MiB")  // "4 MiB"
SRC
    }
  }
}
